{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update-29.json\",\"summary\":\"Submitting the read-index control that tests the scoping statement about which entry points the disarmed proposal gate covers. It is a successor of the flags experiment in the parent investigation: the same three-node Node-API cluster is driven through remove-3 and add-3 so node 3's gate is disarmed, node 3 then calls ReadIndex with a fixed request context and the harness waits for the matching read state to appear in its Ready stream, and afterwards node 3 calls Propose with a bounded context. Three comparisons cover the read state's arrival, the proposal not returning, and its payload not being committed, with admissions on uniquely named invocation events so no comparison can see another operation's result. A local run reproduces exactly the predicted asymmetry: the read state arrives with read index 3 while the member is a voter with leader 1 and its gate disarmed, and in the same run the proposal had not returned after 800 ms inside a 900 ms context and its payload was committed nowhere. The submission is validated with execution requested; its receipt will confirm that the defect is confined to the MsgProp entry points rather than to the member's participation in general.\"}"}}
